      "id": 1,
      "text": "Tubac was founded as a Spanish frontier fort in 1752, making it Arizona's first state park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tubacaz.com/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town's name comes from the O'odham word Cuwak, meaning 'place of dark water,' later Hispanicized to Tubaca.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tubac%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1775, Juan Bautista de Anza departed from Tubac's plaza to lead settlers westward to found San Francisco.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tubacaz.com/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Painter Dale Nichols opened an art school in Tubac in 1948, restoring historic buildings and sparking a modern arts scene.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tubac%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Tubac Presidio State Historic Park preserves the remains of the original Spanish presidio, offering interpretive exhibits of early frontier life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tubac%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The town endured repeated Apache attacks in the 1840s, forcing Sonoran Mexicans to abandon Tubac and nearby Tumacacori.",
